# TEXX SOCIAL — environment variables
#
# The frontend (public/) needs NO build-time environment variables: its
# Supabase URL and publishable key are public by design and live directly
# in public/js/config.js (see docs/SECURITY.md for why that's safe).
#
# Everything below is used only by Supabase Edge Functions (server-side)
# and local tooling. NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in a .env file
# that a frontend build step could read, and never commit a real .env file.

# --- Supabase project (server-side tooling / CI) ---------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
# SERVER ONLY. Grants full database access bypassing RLS. Set this via
# `supabase secrets set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...`, never in a checked-in file.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Local Supabase CLI stack (set automatically by `supabase start`) ------
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:54322/postgres

# --- Optional: third-party providers referenced in docs/API.md -------------
# Music search uses Apple's public iTunes Search API directly from the
# browser and needs no API key. If a paid/authenticated music provider is
# added later, its key belongs here (server-side proxy only, never in
# public/js/config.js):
# MUSIC_PROVIDER_KEY=

# Transactional email (password reset, signup confirmation) is handled by
# Supabase Auth's built-in email provider in development. For production
# volume, configure a custom SMTP provider in the Supabase dashboard
# (Authentication → Email Templates → SMTP Settings) rather than here.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_KEY=

APP_URL=https://www.texxsocial.com
